From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: crypto: sun8i-ce - Add ECDSA signing, ECDH P-521 and DH for the H616

The engine signs ECDSA (operation 6: k, p, a, Gx, Gy, n, d, e -> r, s, user
manual 10.1.3.10), multiplies points on P-521 and does any modular
exponentiation of the RSA sizes. Register, below the software
implementations as the other PKC algorithms:
- ecdsa-nist-p192/p256/p384/p521: set_priv_key (the big endian scalar;
  the public key is computed on the engine) and sign, which writes a
  struct ecdsa_raw_sig. The nonce is from RFC 6979, so a signature does
  not depend on the random source at that moment and equals the
  deterministic ECDSA of other implementations. A faulty signature with
  a deterministic nonce gives the key away, so each one is verified with
  ecdsa-generic before it is returned;
- ecdh-nist-p521;
- dh: modular exponentiation for 512 to 4096-bit primes (the RSA
  sizes), dh-generic for other sizes, a peer value not below p and in
  FIPS mode (the SP800-56A checks).

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
